-- DUMBWAITER (ruled 2026-09-21): an en dash (–, U+2013) at the start of a
-- line, where a `--` line comment was meant. Word's AutoFormat turns both
-- ` - ` and ` -- ` into an en dash, so the dash is inherently ambiguous; the
-- per-diagnostic quick fix therefore offers BOTH the arithmetic spelling
-- (`-`) and the comment-starting spelling (`--`), and the whole-document
-- straighten breaks the tie by position -- comment-shaped here, since the
-- dash is the first non-blank character on its line.
--
-- See doc/reference/errors/README.md, "Curly quotes and dashes from a word
-- processor".

DECLARE Person
  HAS age IS A NUMBER

GIVEN p IS A Person
DECIDE `is adult` IF p's age >= 18

– plain comment
